+# Agent Note: Typed tool dictionaries
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-14-typed-tool-dictionaries.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Tools can accept or return dynamically named keys whose values share an explicit type. Boolean object openness either rejects those keys or accepts unvalidated values.
+
+## Decision
+
+Raw schemas accept schema-valued additionalProperties. The schema walker checks nested declarations and cycles; value validation applies the schema only to undeclared keys. Native declarations preserve it. TypeScript and Python render pure dictionaries with typed values. Mixed objects retain named properties with the language-specific limitations documented in the tools README.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+Flattening dictionaries changes tool data. Unconstrained JSON discards value validation. Consumer-only validation leaves the registry and SDK unable to describe the actual tool.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Boolean openness and named-property validation remain unchanged. Tests cover nested values, invalid declarations, prototype-shaped keys and generated types. The typed-tool-dictionary recorded Session pins the native schema. No event or Loop changes.
